WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:05.920
In 1789, Jeremy Bentham asked
one short question about animals.

2
00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.540
Can they suffer?

3
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.380
Long before, the book
of Proverbs had said:

4
00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:13.680
a righteous man respects
the life of his animal.

5
00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:19.950
And in 2018, the Catholic Catechism was
revised to call the death penalty inadmissible.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.410
So on life, death, animals and marriage,
where do Christian and secular ethics

7
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.080
meet, and where do they clash?

8
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:33.180
In this mission, you'll set Catholic,
Protestant and secular views side by side,

9
00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.170
from embryo research to end-of-life care.

10
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.110
Then you'll trace an old
argument about lying,

11
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.100
from Augustine to Kant to Bonhoeffer.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:46.730
Your mission: find out where Christian
and secular ethics meet on life,

13
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.360
death, animals and marriage,
and where they clash.
